"""Hand-authored legal and support copy.

Extracted verbatim from the reviewed pages, then wrapped in the shared
shell by build_site.py. /privacy is registered as Squatch Lift's App Store
privacy URL and /support as its support URL - do not change these paths.
"""

PRIVACY = '<h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.1rem,5.5vw,3.3rem);line-height:1.05;margin-bottom:0.7rem">Privacy Policy</h1>\n    <p class="fig" style="margin-bottom:2rem">SaaSquatch Lab (SaaSquatch Lab LLC) &middot; Effective September 7, 2026</p>\n\n    <p class="lead"><strong>The short version.</strong> We do not sell your data, we do not run ad trackers, and we do not share your information with data brokers. Most of our apps collect nothing at all &mdash; they have no servers and make no network requests. The two apps that do need an account collect only what the product cannot work without.</p>\n\n    <p>This policy explains what each SaaSquatch Lab app collects, why, and what you can do about it. It applies to every app and website we operate, listed below. Where an app has its own more specific policy, that policy is linked and controls for that app.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="at-a-glance">What each app collects</h2>\n    <div class="tbl-wrap">\n    <table>\n      <thead><tr><th>App</th><th>Data collected</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td><a href="#squatch-lift">Squatch Lift</a></td><td><span class="pill none">None</span></td><td>No servers, no network access. All workout data stays on your device.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><a href="#sizesquatch">SizeSquatch</a></td><td><span class="pill none">None</span></td><td>Photos are processed entirely on-device. <a href="/sizesquatch/privacy">Full policy</a></td></tr>\n        <tr><td><a href="#squatch-travel">Squatch Travel</a></td><td><span class="pill none">None</span></td><td>Offline-first; trip data stays on your device. <a href="/squatchtravel/privacy">Full policy</a></td></tr>\n        <tr><td><a href="#squatch-connect">Squatch Connect</a></td><td><span class="pill some">Minimal</span></td><td>No account. Payment handled by Stripe. <a href="/squatch-connect/privacy">Full policy</a></td></tr>\n        <tr><td><a href="#sasquatch-social">Sasquatch Social</a></td><td><span class="pill some">Account</span></td><td>A social network &mdash; requires an account and stores what you post.</td></tr>\n        <tr><td><a href="#app-tracker">App Tracker</a></td><td><span class="pill some">Account</span></td><td>Stores the job applications and documents you create.</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n    </div>\n\n    <h2 id="on-device">Apps that collect nothing</h2>\n    <p>These apps have no backend of our own, no analytics SDK, no advertising SDK, and no third&nbsp;party trackers. They do not transmit your content anywhere.</p>\n\n    <h3 id="squatch-lift">Squatch Lift</h3>\n    <p>Squatch Lift is an on-device workout tracker. Your workouts, exercise history, personal records, body measurements, supplement log, and any selfie you attach to a share card are stored locally on your device using Apple\'s on-device database and never leave it. We operate no server for this app and receive none of this information. Uninstalling the app deletes this data from your device.</p>\n    <p>Squatch Lift offers an optional auto&#8209;renewing subscription (Squatch Lift Pro). Purchases are processed entirely by Apple &mdash; we never see your payment details. See <a href="#purchases">Purchases and subscriptions</a> and our <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a>.</p>\n\n    <h3 id="sizesquatch">SizeSquatch</h3>\n    <p>SizeSquatch resizes and crops photos entirely on your device. It uses the system photo picker, so it can only ever access the specific photos you select &mdash; never your whole library. Exported images go only where you send them. The app makes no network connections of its own. See the <a href="/sizesquatch/privacy">SizeSquatch privacy policy</a> for detail.</p>\n\n    <h3 id="squatch-travel">Squatch Travel</h3>\n    <p>Squatch Travel is built to work with no connectivity. Your itinerary, reservations, phrasebooks, and destination guides are downloaded and then stored on your device. Your travel plans are not uploaded to us. See the <a href="/squatchtravel/privacy">Squatch Travel privacy policy</a>.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="minimal">Apps that collect the minimum</h2>\n\n    <h3 id="squatch-connect">Squatch Connect</h3>\n    <p>Squatch Connect sells travel eSIM data plans. There is no user account. To deliver a plan we process the destination and plan you choose and an email address for your receipt and eSIM details. Payment is handled by Stripe, our payment processor &mdash; we never receive or store your card number. Our connectivity partner provisions the eSIM profile itself. We do not collect your passport, identity documents, location history, or browsing activity. See the <a href="/squatch-connect/privacy">Squatch Connect privacy policy</a>.</p>\n\n    <h3 id="sasquatch-social">Sasquatch Social</h3>\n    <p>Sasquatch Social is a social network, so it necessarily stores what you choose to publish. We collect:</p>\n    <ul>\n      <li><strong>Account information</strong> &mdash; your email address and password (stored hashed), display name, and profile details you add.</li>\n      <li><strong>Content you create</strong> &mdash; posts, comments, messages, listings, poll votes, events, and uploaded media.</li>\n      <li><strong>Social graph</strong> &mdash; who you follow, block, or mute.</li>\n      <li><strong>Identity verification</strong> &mdash; if you choose to verify your identity, our verification provider (Didit, or Stripe Identity as a fallback) processes your government ID and returns only a pass/fail result and your verified legal name. <strong>We never receive or store images of your ID.</strong> Verification is handled under that provider\'s own privacy policy.</li>\n      <li><strong>Operational logs</strong> &mdash; minimal server logs needed to keep the service running and to investigate abuse.</li>\n    </ul>\n    <p>We do not build advertising profiles, we do not run third&#8209;party ad trackers in the app, and we do not sell or rent your information. Dating features are off unless you turn them on.</p>\n\n    <h3 id="app-tracker">App Tracker</h3>\n    <p>App Tracker stores the job applications, resumes, cover letters, and notes you create so they sync across your devices. When you use an AI writing feature, the text you submit is sent to our AI provider to generate the requested document. That content is not used to train third&#8209;party models. We do not share your job search with employers, recruiters, or anyone else.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="purchases">Purchases and subscriptions</h2>\n    <p>All in&#8209;app purchases and subscriptions are processed by Apple (App Store) or Google (Google Play). <strong>We never receive your payment card details.</strong> We receive only the confirmation that a purchase or subscription is valid. Web purchases (Squatch Connect) are processed by Stripe under Stripe\'s privacy policy. Subscriptions are managed and cancelled in your App Store or Google Play account settings, not by us.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="never">What we never do</h2>\n    <ul>\n      <li>We never sell, rent, or trade your personal information.</li>\n      <li>We never share your information with data brokers.</li>\n      <li>We do not embed third&#8209;party advertising SDKs or cross&#8209;app tracking SDKs in our apps.</li>\n      <li>We do not use your content to build advertising profiles.</li>\n      <li>We do not request tracking permission, because we do not track you across other companies\' apps and websites.</li>\n    </ul>\n\n    <h2 id="retention">How long we keep things</h2>\n    <p>On&#8209;device data lives on your device until you delete it or uninstall the app; we have no copy. For account&#8209;based apps, we keep your content while your account is open and delete it within 30 days of account deletion, except where we must retain records to comply with law or to resolve a dispute. Operational logs are kept on a short rolling schedule and then discarded.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="rights">Your rights</h2>\n    <p>Wherever you live, you may ask us to give you a copy of your data, correct it, or delete it. If you are in the EU/EEA or UK, you additionally have rights to restrict or object to processing and to data portability under the GDPR. If you are a California resident, you have the rights to know, delete, correct, and opt out of sale or sharing under the CCPA/CPRA &mdash; and we can tell you plainly that <strong>we do not sell or share personal information</strong> as those terms are defined. We will not discriminate against you for exercising any of these rights.</p>\n    <p>To make a request, email <a href="mailto:hello@saasquatchlab.com">hello@saasquatchlab.com</a>. Sasquatch Social users can also use the in&#8209;app data rights tools at <a href="https://www.sasquatchsocial.com/privacy/data-rights">sasquatchsocial.com/privacy/data-rights</a>. For apps that store nothing off your device, there is nothing for us to return or delete &mdash; deleting the app removes the data.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="children">Children</h2>\n    <p>Our apps are not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from them. If you believe a child has provided us information, contact us and we will delete it.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="security">Security</h2>\n    <p>Data in transit is encrypted with TLS. Account data is held in access&#8209;controlled managed infrastructure with row&#8209;level authorization, and passwords are stored hashed. No system is perfect, but the most reliable protection we offer is structural: most of our apps never collect your data in the first place.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="international">Where data is processed</h2>\n    <p>SaaSquatch Lab LLC operates in the United States, and account data for our server&#8209;backed apps is processed there. If you use our apps from outside the United States, you understand that your information is processed in the United States.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>\n    <p>If we change this policy we will update the effective date above, and for material changes we will give notice in the affected app. Continued use after a change means you accept the updated policy.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>\n    <p>SaaSquatch Lab LLC &mdash; Pacific Northwest, United States<br />\n    <a href="mailto:hello@saasquatchlab.com">hello@saasquatchlab.com</a></p>'

SUPPORT = '<h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.1rem,5.5vw,3.3rem);line-height:1.05;margin-bottom:0.7rem">Support</h1>\n    <p class="fig" style="margin-bottom:2rem">We\'re a small team and we read everything. Email <a href="mailto:hello@saasquatchlab.com">hello@saasquatchlab.com</a> and we\'ll get back to you as soon as we can.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="sizesquatch">SizeSquatch: Photo Resizer</h2>\n\n    <h3>Are my photos uploaded anywhere?</h3>\n    <p>No. Every resize, crop, and grid is processed entirely on your device. SizeSquatch has no servers, no accounts, and no analytics — your photos never leave your phone. See the full <a href="/sizesquatch/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>\n\n    <h3>How does the free version work?</h3>\n    <p>The free version includes 3 exports with every feature available. A one-time purchase unlocks unlimited exports forever — there is no subscription.</p>\n\n    <h3>I purchased the unlock but it shows as locked.</h3>\n    <p>Open SizeSquatch → Settings (gear icon) → <strong>Restore Purchases</strong>. Make sure you\'re signed in with the same Apple Account you purchased with. The unlock supports Family Sharing, so family members can restore it too.</p>\n\n    <h3>How do refunds work?</h3>\n    <p>Purchases are processed by Apple, so refunds go through them: visit <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com">reportaproblem.apple.com</a>, sign in, and choose the purchase.</p>\n\n    <h3>My exported photo looks cropped differently than I expected.</h3>\n    <p>SizeSquatch fills the target frame completely so there are never white bars. Drag the preview to reposition and pinch to zoom before exporting — what you see in the preview is exactly what gets exported.</p>\n\n    <h3>Does it really work for passport photos?</h3>\n    <p>Yes — the Passport &amp; ID presets produce correctly sized files (for example, US 2×2 in at 600×600 px, 300 DPI) and show the official framing rules. You\'re responsible for meeting the photo-quality rules (lighting, background, expression), so review the guidance shown in the app before submitting to an agency.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="social">Sasquatch Social</h2>\n    <p>For help with Sasquatch Social, visit <a href="https://www.sasquatchsocial.com/support">sasquatchsocial.com/support</a>.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="other">App Tracker</h2>\n    <p>Support for <a href="https://saasquatchapptracker.com">App Tracker</a> is available in each product, or email us at the address above.</p>'

TERMS = '<h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.1rem,5.5vw,3.3rem);line-height:1.05;margin-bottom:0.7rem">Terms of Use</h1>\n    <p class="fig" style="margin-bottom:2rem">End User License Agreement &middot; SaaSquatch Lab LLC &middot; Effective September 7, 2026</p>\n\n    <p class="lead">These terms govern your use of SaaSquatch Lab apps and websites. By downloading or using any of our apps, you agree to them. If you do not agree, do not use the apps.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="license">1. Licence</h2>\n    <p>We grant you a personal, limited, non&#8209;exclusive, non&#8209;transferable, revocable licence to use our apps on devices you own or control, for your own personal or internal business use, in accordance with the usage rules of the app store you obtained the app from. This licence does not transfer ownership. All rights not expressly granted are reserved.</p>\n    <p>You may not reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble the apps except to the extent that restriction is prohibited by law; rent, lease, sell, sublicense, or redistribute them; or remove any proprietary notices.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="subscriptions">2. Purchases and subscriptions</h2>\n    <p>Some apps offer paid unlocks or auto&#8209;renewing subscriptions. Current products:</p>\n    <div class="tbl-wrap">\n    <table>\n      <thead><tr><th>Product</th><th>Type</th><th>Price</th></tr></thead>\n      <tbody>\n        <tr><td>Squatch Lift Pro &mdash; Monthly</td><td>Auto&#8209;renewing subscription</td><td>$4.99 / month</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Squatch Lift Pro &mdash; Yearly</td><td>Auto&#8209;renewing subscription</td><td>$29.99 / year</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>SizeSquatch &mdash; Unlock Everything</td><td>One&#8209;time purchase</td><td>$4.99</td></tr>\n        <tr><td>Squatch Connect data plans</td><td>One&#8209;time purchase</td><td>Varies by destination</td></tr>\n      </tbody>\n    </table>\n    </div>\n    <p>Prices are in U.S. dollars and may differ by storefront. Squatch Lift is free to use for your first three completed workouts; Pro is optional and unlocks unlimited use.</p>\n\n    <h3 id="renewal">Auto&#8209;renewal terms</h3>\n    <ul>\n      <li>Payment is charged to your App Store or Google Play account at confirmation of purchase.</li>\n      <li>A subscription <strong>automatically renews</strong> at the same price for the same period unless auto&#8209;renew is turned off <strong>at least 24 hours before the end of the current period</strong>.</li>\n      <li>Your account is charged for renewal within 24 hours prior to the end of the current period.</li>\n      <li>You can manage or cancel a subscription in your <strong>App Store or Google Play account settings</strong> at any time. We cannot cancel it for you.</li>\n      <li>Cancelling stops future renewals; it does not refund the current period. Any unused portion of a free trial is forfeited when you buy a subscription.</li>\n    </ul>\n    <p>Refunds are handled by Apple or Google under their policies, not by us. If a purchase went wrong, contact us at <a href="mailto:hello@saasquatchlab.com">hello@saasquatchlab.com</a> and we will help where we can.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="acceptable">3. Acceptable use</h2>\n    <p>You agree not to use our apps or services to break the law, harass or threaten anyone, post content you have no right to post, impersonate others, scrape or overload our services, attempt to gain unauthorised access, or circumvent security or payment controls.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="content">4. Your content</h2>\n    <p>Where an app lets you publish content &mdash; principally Sasquatch Social &mdash; you keep ownership of what you create. You grant us only the licence we need to host, store, transmit, and display that content in order to operate the service. You are responsible for what you publish. We may remove content or suspend accounts that violate these terms or our community standards.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="privacy">5. Privacy</h2>\n    <p>Our handling of your information is described in our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, which forms part of these terms. Most of our apps collect nothing at all.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="availability">6. Availability and changes</h2>\n    <p>We may add, change, or discontinue features. We aim to give reasonable notice before removing something you rely on. We do not guarantee uninterrupted or error&#8209;free operation.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="warranty">7. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>\n    <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, the apps and services are provided <strong>&ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as available&rdquo; without warranties of any kind</strong>, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non&#8209;infringement. Some jurisdictions do not allow the exclusion of implied warranties, so parts of this section may not apply to you.</p>\n    <p>Squatch Lift is a fitness logging tool, not medical advice. Squatch Travel and Squatch Connect provide travel information and connectivity but are not a substitute for official government, airline, or emergency sources. Verify safety&#8209;critical information independently.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="liability">8. Limitation of liability</h2>\n    <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, SaaSquatch Lab LLC is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits or lost data. Our total liability for any claim relating to an app is limited to the amount you paid us for that app in the twelve months before the claim, or $50, whichever is greater.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="termination">9. Termination</h2>\n    <p>You may stop using the apps at any time by deleting them. We may suspend or terminate access if you materially breach these terms. Sections that by their nature should survive termination do so.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="apple">10. App store terms</h2>\n    <p>For apps obtained from the Apple App Store: this agreement is between you and SaaSquatch Lab LLC only, <strong>not with Apple</strong>. Apple is not responsible for the app or its content. Apple has no obligation to provide maintenance or support. If the app fails to conform to any applicable warranty, you may notify Apple and Apple will refund the purchase price; to the maximum extent permitted by law, Apple has no other warranty obligation. SaaSquatch Lab LLC is responsible for addressing any claims relating to the app, including product liability, legal compliance, and intellectual property claims. You represent that you are not located in a country subject to a U.S. Government embargo or designated as terrorist&#8209;supporting, and are not on any U.S. Government prohibited&#8209;party list. <strong>Apple and its subsidiaries are third&#8209;party beneficiaries of this agreement and may enforce it against you.</strong> Equivalent terms apply to Google LLC for apps obtained from Google Play.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="law">11. Governing law</h2>\n    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Washington, United States, without regard to its conflict of laws rules. Nothing here removes consumer protection rights you have under the mandatory law of your country of residence.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="changes">12. Changes to these terms</h2>\n    <p>We may update these terms. We will change the effective date above and, for material changes, give notice in the affected app. Continued use after a change means you accept the updated terms.</p>\n\n    <h2 id="contact">13. Contact</h2>\n    <p>SaaSquatch Lab LLC &mdash; Pacific Northwest, United States<br />\n    <a href="mailto:hello@saasquatchlab.com">hello@saasquatchlab.com</a></p>'

